<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43000" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scissĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		scindo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That may easily be split</i>, <i>cleft</i>, or <i>rent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alumen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
					2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					6, 6, 30</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Postclass.) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scissus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>rent</i>, <i>torn</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palliastrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 104, 27</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centunculus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9, p. 222, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fasciae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 3, 47, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
